At level 35, the player can also catch the [[Snowy knight]] butterfly, which are often in the same areas.

For slightly higher experience rates, players may choose to trap [[Cerulean twitch]] at the same time as netting butterflies. Simply set up two bird traps and catch butterflies while waiting.

=== Levels 39–43: Embertailed jerboas ===
From level 39 to 43, catch [[Embertailed jerboa|embertailed jerboas]] at [[Locus Oasis]]. Fairy ring {{Fairycode|AJP}} is right next to the hunter area. With 3 traps you can reach 50,000 experience per hour.

=== Levels 43–46: Falconry ===
[[File:Spotted_kebbit_spawn.png|alt=Ideal spotted kebbit training area with three spawn points in the south-eastern corner.|thumb|Ideal spotted kebbit training area with three spawn points in the south-eastern corner.]]
From level 43 to 49, catch [[Spotted kebbit|spotted kebbits]] (and [[Dark kebbit|dark kebbits]] at level 57) using the [[falconry]] technique. To do this, enter the [[Piscatoris falconry area]] east of the fairy ring {{Fairycode|AKQ}} and rent a [[gyr falcon]] for 500 coins. The weapon, shield, and hands slots must be empty for this. Head to the south-eastern area and click on the kebbits to send the falcon towards the kebbit. When the falcon catches the kebbit, retrieve the falcon and the loot, and drop the loot afterwards. To minimise downtime, stand close to the kebbit or the spawn tile before using the falcon.

Wear weight-reducing clothing to reduce run energy drain, and bring a stamina potion to restore run energy. The [[bonecrusher]] will automatically bury the bones from the kebbits, which reduces dropping.

The following rates can be expected while training here:

* [[Spotted kebbit|Spotted kebbits]] (43-57) give 60,000 up to 70,000. You can reduce the amount of run energy used to catch spotted kebbits by focusing on their three spawn points located at the south-eastern corner of the falconry area. Spotted kebbits will respawn 4 seconds after being retrieved by the player.
* [[Dark kebbit|Dark kebbits]] (57-60+) give 75,000 up to 80,000. Spawn points for dark kebbits are spread throughout the edges of the falconry area. The two spawn points closest to each other are on the west edge of the area. Dark kebbits will respawn 4 seconds after being retrieved by the player.
* [[Dashing kebbit|Dashing kebbits]] (69+) give 85,000 up to 95,000. Since dashing kebbits do not become available until level 69, training with them is not popular since salamanders offer better experience rates from level 60 onwards.

==Other methods==
While the following methods can all be completed while on a [[Hunter Rumour]], they might be worth considering beyond this.

===Level 60+: Orange salamanders===
[[Orange salamander (Hunter)|Orange salamanders]] are caught using traps on [[Young tree|Young trees]]. With partial completion of [[Beneath Cursed Sands]] one can access the [[Necropolis Hunter area]], using 4 traps at once, you can expect more than 40,000xp an hour with minimal attention. To prolong trips, it is recommended to bring multiple [[Waterskin|Waterskins]] or the [[Circlet of water]] and wear [[Desert clothing]]. There are also three nearby waterskin spawns to the east. Each trap requires a [[Small fishing net]] and a [[Rope]]. Both can be stored in the [[Huntsman's kit]].

===Level 69+: Dashing kebbits===
[[Dashing kebbits]] are caught using Falconry. [[Dashing kebbit meat]] is the third highest healing food (surpassed only by [[cooked moonlight antelope]] and [[marlin]]) and restores 10 run energy; gathering the meat with a [[meat pouch]] is reasonably quick.

===Level 72/91+: Sunlight/Moonlight antelopes===
Both [[sunlight antelope|sunlight]] and [[moonlight antelopes]] can be caught via pitfall trapping, offering up to 135,000xp per hour, ammunition for the [[hunters' sunlight crossbow]] and [[hunter meat|antelope meat]] which can be cooked after 50 [[Hunter Rumours]] have been completed. As antelope meat provides incredibly high healing per inventory slot and [[antler bolts]] cannot be obtained anywhere else, hunting these outside of Rumours might be desirable.

===Level 75+: Moonlight moths===
[[Moonlight moths]] can be caught with a [[butterfly jar]], and can subsequently be combined with any raw [[hunter meat]] to provide a 2 dose [[moonlight moth mix]] which restores 22 prayer points per dose, as an alternative to [[prayer potions]] when inventory space is not a limitation.

